  "caption_groups": [
    {
      "start": 0.852083,
      "end": 2.857291,
      "text": "Volcanoes are vents where molten rock"
    },
    {
      "start": 2.870333,
      "end": 5.096916,
      "text": "material emerges from the Earth’s interior"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.122916,
      "end": 6.060458,
      "text": "during an eruption."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.792083000000001,
      "end": 9.367624000000001,
      "text": "The form and style of an eruption"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.380625,
      "end": 11.151458,
      "text": "of a volcano is determined by the"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.1645,
      "end": 12.531708,
      "text": "composition of the lava."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.852083,
      "end": 16.078666000000002,
      "text": "Volcanoes are referred to as either active"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.104708,
      "end": 17.979708,
      "text": "or dormant based on their frequency of"
    },
    {
      "start": 18.00575,
      "end": 19.411998999999998,
      "text": "eruption or volcanism."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.752083000000002,
      "end": 23.134916000000004,
      "text": "Superheated magma rises through the mantle"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.147916000000002,
      "end": 24.814625,
      "text": "and melts the crust above to flow"
    },
    {
      "start": 24.840625000000003,
      "end": 25.647916000000002,
      "text": "on the surface."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.980083000000004,
      "end": 28.881166000000004,
      "text": "If there is evidence for magma beneath"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.907166000000004,
      "end": 31.211874000000005,
      "text": "the ground, the volcano should be considered"
    },
    {
      "start": 31.237916000000006,
      "end": 31.732707000000005,
      "text": "active."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.064083000000004,
      "end": 35.290666,
      "text": "Volcanologists found that an eruption was"
    },
    {
      "start": 35.316708000000006,
      "end": 37.66045700000001,
      "text": "likely triggered by magma taking a nonstop"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.673458000000004,
      "end": 38.702124000000005,
      "text": "route from the mantle."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.036083,
      "end": 42.067375,
      "text": "Stromboli is a volcano that has been"
    },
    {
      "start": 42.093374999999995,
      "end": 44.450165999999996,
      "text": "erupting nearly continuously for centuries"
    },
    {
      "start": 44.476208,
      "end": 45.674124,
      "text": "in a specific style."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.00808299999999,
      "end": 48.37529099999999,
      "text": "The Pu‘ u‘ ō‘ ō eruption began"
    },
    {
      "start": 48.37529099999999,
      "end": 48.72529099999999,
      "text": "in 1983,"
    },
    {
      "start": 49.75549999999999,
      "end": 51.30499999999999,
      "text": "and ranks as the longest and most"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.33099999999999,
      "end": 53.27112399999999,
      "text": "voluminous known outpouring of lava from"
    },
    {
      "start": 53.29716599999999,
      "end": 55.44562399999999,
      "text": "Kīlauea Volcano's East Rift Zone in more"
    },
    {
      "start": 55.45862499999999,
      "end": 55.90569433333333,
      "text": "than 500 years."
    }
  ],
